            "text": "{\"study_topic_id\":\"study-78e3a6aad21c9f5f14e5\",\"overview\":{\"text\":\"The 1972 film The Godfather is Francis Ford Coppola’s crime drama, adapted from Mario Puzo’s novel. It follows New York crime boss Don Vito Corleone and his son Michael (Al Pacino), whose gradual rise to family leadership tests loyalty and power. Marlon Brando plays Vito. A distinctive sequence intercuts Michael’s participation in his sister’s baby’s baptism with killings of rival leaders, contrasting religious vows with violent business. The film helped shape the American gangster movie and remains culturally important: the Academy named it Best Picture for films released in 1972, and the Library of Congress added it to the National Film Registry in 1990.\",\"source_urls\":[\"https://catalog.afi.com/Catalog/moviedetails/54023\",\"https://www.oscars.org/oscars/ceremonies/1973/H\",\"https://www.loc.gov/static/programs/national-film-preservation-board/documents/Registry-Titles-alphabetically.pdf\"]},\"key_facts\":[{\"text\":\"Francis Ford Coppola directed the film and co-wrote its screenplay with Mario Puzo; Marlon Brando and Al Pacino star as Vito and Michael Corleone.\",\"source_urls\":[\"https://catalog.afi.com/Catalog/moviedetails/54023\"]},{\"text\":\"The story is adapted from Mario Puzo’s crime novel and centers on the Corleone family.\",\"source_urls\":[\"https://catalog.afi.com/Catalog/moviedetails/54023\",\"https://www.oscars.org/collection-highlights/godfather\"]},{\"text\":\"In a signature montage, scenes of Michael at a baptism are intercut with the murders of his family’s rivals.\",\"source_urls\":[\"https://catalog.afi.com/Catalog/moviedetails/54023\"]},{\"text\":\"At the 1973 Academy Awards, honoring movies released in 1972, The Godfather won Best Picture.\",\"source_urls\":[\"https://www.oscars.org/oscars/ceremonies/1973/H\"]},{\"text\":\"The Library of Congress’s National Film Registry list records The Godfather as inducted in 1990.\",\"source_urls\":[\"https://www.loc.gov/static/programs/national-film-preservation-board/documents/Registry-Titles-alphabetically.pdf\"]}],\"sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Godfather (1972)\",\"url\":\"https://catalog.afi.com/Catalog/moviedetails/54023\",\"publisher\":\"American Film Institute, AFI Catalog of Feature Films\",\"retrieved_at\":\"2026-09-24T18:43:20.443527+00:00\",\"supports\":\"Release details, director, writers, cast, adaptation, story, ending, and baptism montage.\"},{\"title\":\"The 45th Academy Awards | 1973\",\"url\":\"https://www.oscars.org/oscars/ceremonies/1973/H\",\"publisher\":\"Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences\",\"retrieved_at\":\"2026-09-24T18:43:20.443527+00:00\",\"supports\":\"The Godfather’s Best Picture win at the 1973 ceremony honoring 1972 films.\"},{\"title\":\"National Film Registry Titles Selected 1989-2017, Listed Alphabetically\",\"url\":\"https://www.loc.gov/static/programs/national-film-preservation-board/documents/Registry-Titles-alphabetically.pdf\",\"publisher\":\"Library of Congress, National Film Preservation Board\",\"retrieved_at\":\"2026-09-24T18:43:20.443527+00:00\",\"supports\":\"The film’s 1972 release year and 1990 Registry induction.\"}],\"research_queries\":[\"site:afi.com The Godfather 1972 Francis Ford Coppola film catalog\",\"site:loc.gov The Godfather 1972 National Film Registry\",\"site:oscars.org The Godfather 1972 awards film\"],\"notes\":\"The AFI catalog supports the film’s identity, credits, plot, and distinguishing montage; the Academy and Library of Congress pages independently support its award and preservation significance.\",\"unresolved_concerns\":[],\"self_check_complete\":true}"
          }
